orca-mobile: Hey CS  onboarding for Orca app. After updating to embeddings flow, our iOS build sees a burst of 429s during first-run onboarding. No heavy user load, just 10 QA devices.

orca-mobile: Quick snippet from device logs:
```
[2026-04-12T09:12:01Z] preflight GET /v1/preflight 200 ok
[2026-04-12T09:12:01Z] POST /v1/handshake 401 x-client-id=device:qn12
[2026-04-12T09:12:01Z] POST /v1/handshake 429 rate_limiter:preflight
[2026-04-12T09:12:02Z] POST /v1/handshake 429 rate_limiter:preflight
[2026-04-12T09:12:03Z] POST /v1/handshake 429 rate_limiter:preflight
```

orca-mobile: We're using redwood-mobile-sdk v0.7.0. App does token fetch in AppDelegate and again in background sync task; also a service worker-like background process triggers `Redwood.init()` on wake. Possible double-init?

maria_cs: thanks  looks like a classic multi-process/token fanout. Mobile + background sync + service worker all racing to refresh ephemeral tokens. What's your ephemeral token TTL?

orca-mobile: TTL=45s currently (short for security). We found ServiceWorkerStart and AppResume both call `init()` without coordination.

leo_se: quick repro: create 3 concurrent init() calls -> each requests preflight, some get 401 as auth not ready, then retry loops create rapid preflight QPS -> 429s. Fixes: single-source token provider or an in-process lock, and add splay to background tasks. Example pattern: use BroadcastChannel (or local singleton) to serialize token refresh on iOS. Pseudocode:
```
// singleton token broker
async function getEphemeralToken() {
  if (cache.valid) return cache.token;
  if (refreshInProgress) return await waitForToken();
  refreshInProgress = true;
  const t = await auth.fetchEphemeral();
  cache = { token: t, expiresAt: now + 120000 };
  refreshInProgress = false;
  notifyWaiters(t);
  return t;
}
```
Also prefer TTL >= 120s for onboarding/dev to avoid frequent refreshes.

maria_cs: infra note  we can temporarily raise preflight quota for account orca-inc for the demo. Need confirmation.

orca-mobile: would appreciate a temporary bump for next 24hrs. We'll implement client locking and longer TTL today.

ratelimit-bot: Account orca-inc preflight quota has an automated alert: 5xx/429 spike detected. Recommend applying temporary QPS increase or advise client fixes.

infra-bot: @orca-mobile  applied temporary preflight QPS bump to 60 for orca-inc until 2026-04-13T09:12:00Z. We'll watch for anomalous growth. :eyes:

leo_se: also add client-side backoff on 429s, cap retries and add jitter. For mobile we recommend exponential backoff with base 100ms, cap 2s, and abort after 6 attempts.

orca-mobile: implemented broker + splay + backoff. Re-ran onboarding flow on 12 devices in parallel  stable, only 1-2 transient 429s during peak. Good enough for demo. Thanks.

maria_cs: follow-ups: 1) Orca to paste init/token broker snippet to thread, 2) Redwood to share mobile preflight best-practices doc, 3) Infra will auto-revert quota bump at expiry unless flagged. I'll schedule a 20-min handoff to review.

orca-mobile: posting snippet now and pinging when demo complete. :thumbsup:
